cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the associated manuscript."
title: "Are published immune-checkpoint-blockade response signatures reproducible? A pre-registered negative study in melanoma"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered, multi-cohort reproducibility study of published immune
  checkpoint blockade response signatures in melanoma using exclusively public
  data. Two signatures with mathematically different constructions and
  independent origins both failed to reproduce their published performance in
  independent cohorts, while four standard technical explanations for a negative
  result were each tested and excluded.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-07"
keywords:
  - melanoma
  - immune checkpoint blockade
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - bioinformatics
